  "query_preview": ".. (Wednesday through Saturday) \n\nAs high pressure settles over the mid Atlantic States on Tue\nanother northern stream short wave/trof tracks eastward across \nsouthern Canada pushing a weak cold front se thru central IL on \nWed afternoon. This front to pass through dry as well with model\nguidance keeping qpf even further north/ne of IL than this \nweekend system. Milder highs in the upper 70s to around 80F on \nWed and these milder high temps in upper 70s/lower 80s likely \ncontinues Thu and Friday. 500 mb heights slowly rise to between \n584-586 decameters by late Friday into Saturday with dry weather\nlikely continuing with warm highs in the low to mid 80s next \nweekend. We may be getting into elevated field fire risk from \nWed thru Saturday with the warmer temps and lower humidity \nlevels especially in southeast IL where afternoon Minimum RH's \nget to 30% or less starting Wed, though winds are forecast to \nremain fairly light much of next week. As of Sep 28th, 21% of \nsoybeans and 26% of corn has been harvested over IL, so well \ninto the fall harvest season.",
